# Nachtschicht review checklist

Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` before structural changes and update it (module map, status section) when you add, move, or finish something.

## Safety invariants (never break)
- AI output is a verdict only. Twitch actions go through `lib/policy.ts` then `lib/twitch.ts`.
- Title, category, tags: proposal only, published after broadcaster approval.
- Protected roles are flagged, never punished automatically.
- Shadow mode and `emergencyStop` hold every action; held actions are still audited.
- Unban is human-only. The AI must not undo its own bans.
- Chat text is untrusted. `!aimod` commands only from a verified broadcaster (user ID/badge), never from message content alone.
- Every decision writes an audit record with model and rule version. Bump `RULE_VERSION` when policy behavior changes.

## Before finishing any task
- `npm test` passes; add or update tests in `lib/*.test.ts` for policy, command parsing, and signature changes.
- `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run lint` are clean; check ReadLints on edited files.
- New `DashboardSnapshot` or `ChannelSettings` fields are filled in `lib/db.ts`, `lib/moderation.ts`, the dashboard, and test fixtures.
- Schema changes use `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` or `ensureColumn`; never break an existing local `data/nachtschicht.sqlite`.
- API routes validate input with zod and return a 4xx JSON error instead of throwing.

## Twitch integration
- No secrets or tokens in code, logs, or git. Tokens are stored via `lib/crypto.ts`.
- OAuth `state` is created with `saveOauthState` and checked once with `consumeOauthState`.
- EventSub: verify signature and timestamp, deduplicate with `rememberEvent`, answer the verification challenge.
- Request only the scopes listed in `getTwitchConfig`; adding a scope means updating the architecture doc.
- Without credentials the app must stay in demo mode and never call Twitch.

## Conventions
- Code, comments, logs, commit messages, and docs (`docs/`, `README.md`, this rule): English. User-facing dashboard text: English.
- Keep route handlers thin; logic lives in `lib/`.
- Verify UI changes in the browser (`npm run dev`, http://localhost:3000).
